You already have the Bell, so AFAIK there's nothing you can do aside
from dying to make the game unwinnable.  Certainly nothing of the "I
did this and that in the wrong order and suddenly the game's done"
nature, though things like getting cornered naked and equipmentless by
a bunch of minotaurs could be disastrous.

There is one thing that you shouldn't do until you're all prepped to
finish the game, but I don't know that I should mention it.   (qba'g
jnxr Ebqarl hc hagvy lbh'ir tbg gur pnaqrynoehz, oryy, 7 pnaqyrf, naq
unir znexrq gur ivoengvat fdhner)

> I appreciate that I have a whole bunch of killing to do ahead before the
> end is reached; just wondering if it's something you have to figure out by
> trial and error or do you get help?

The Oracle is there to help.  Really the main thing that's pretty tough
to figure out is what to do at the vibrating square.  You already know
about the book, if you explore carefully you should find all you need
before the square...the exploration may be boring, though, depending on
how souped up you are and what nasties haven't gone the way of the dodo.



